    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "281ba04a_e07a158c",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/emul/emul_pdc.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-24T18:03:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see your point, but there may be scenarios where I don\u0027t want to trigger multiple interrupts.  I may need to configure multiple items then want the emulator to notify the driver something changed.  Maybe something like\n\n```\nset_capability(...);\nset_connector_capability(...);\nset_connector_status(...);\npulse_irq(...); \n```\n\nBut also testing\n```\nset_capability(...);\npulse_irq(...); \nset_connector_capability(...);\npulse_irq(...); \nset_connector_status(...);\npulse_irq(...); \n```\nWould be worthwhile too.  \n\nI think having some control from the test framework on when to notify the driver is needed.  Maybe this backend API should be renamed to something like `commit_changes` or `notify_driver`.  Thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "65a7f0f9_986f3e8a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "6459b98b399edafb51279af9a73d675876961598",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73544142_28a3d43e",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/emul/emul_pdc.h",
